 * UTF-8 encode `text` and render it exactly like CPython's `repr(bytes)`.
 *
 * CPython prefers single quotes, switching to double quotes only when the
 * data contains a single quote but no double quote. Bytes are shown
 * literally when printable ASCII; quote/backslash are escaped; \t \n \r
 * have named escapes; everything else becomes \xhh (lowercase).
 */
